@startuml ssd5-make-availability
title SSD - Make Availability (success and failure scenarios)
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor ":AdministrativeStaff" as staff
participant ":System" as sys

note over staff, sys : Precondition: user (administrative staff, or the healthcare professional\nfor their own availability) is identified and authenticated;\nthe professional and the clinic location exist

loop availability not created yet
    staff -> sys : makeAvailability(professionalId, locationId, fromDate, toDate,\ndaysOfWeek, dayOfMonth, startTime, endTime, slotLength)
    alt slots generated (main)
        sys --> staff : created slots,\ntimes skipped because they overlap existing slots
    else professional does not practise at this location (FAILURE)
        sys --> staff : professional does not practise at this location
    else invalid date range, time range or slot length (FAILURE)
        sys --> staff : invalid availability parameters
    else days of week / day of month match no date in the range (FAILURE)
        sys --> staff : no slots generated
    end
end

note over staff, sys : Example: Dr. X, every Monday from 2026-11-01 to 2026-11-30,\n09:00-12:00, 30 min slots -> 5 Mondays x 6 slots = 30 slots

@enduml
